{"id":"hophni","name":"Hophni","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:hophni"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Hophni","text":"Pugilist or client, one of the two sons of Eli, the high priest (1 Sam. 1:3; 2:34), who, because he was “very old,” resigned to them the active duties of his office. By their scandalous conduct they brought down a curse on their father’s house (2:22, 12-27, 27-36; 3:11-14). For their wickedness they were called “sons of Belial,” i.e., worthless men (2:12). They both perished in the disastrous battle with the Philistines at Aphek (4:11). (See PHINEHAS.)"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5941","lemma":"עֵלִי","xlit":"ʻÊlîy","gloss":"Eli, an Israelite highpriest","kjv":"Eli","count":9,"share":0.27},{"strong":"H2652","lemma":"חׇפְנִי","xlit":"Chophnîy","gloss":"Chophni, an Israelite","kjv":"Hophni","count":5,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H6372","lemma":"פִּינְחָס","xlit":"Pîynᵉchâç","gloss":"Pinechas, the name of three Israelites","kjv":"Phinehas","count":5,"share":0.15},{"strong":"H5288","lemma":"נַעַר","xlit":"naʻar","gloss":"a boy , from the age of infancy to adolescence","kjv":"babe, boy, child, damsel","count":6,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H8050","lemma":"שְׁמוּאֵל","xlit":"Shᵉmûwʼêl","gloss":"Shemuel, the name of three Israelites","kjv":"Samuel, Shemuel","count":4,"share":0.12},{"strong":"H2076","lemma":"זָבַח","xlit":"zâbach","gloss":"to slaughter an animal","kjv":"kill, offer, sacrifice, slay","count":4,"share":0.12}],"verses":["1Sam.1.3","1Sam.2.12","1Sam.2.20","1Sam.2.22","1Sam.2.27","1Sam.3.12","1Sam.3.14","1Sam.4.4","1Sam.4.11","1Sam.2.13","1Sam.2.14","1Sam.2.15","1Sam.2.16","1Sam.2.17","1Sam.2.18","1Sam.2.19","1Sam.2.21","1Sam.2.23","1Sam.2.24","1Sam.2.25","1Sam.2.26","1Sam.2.28","1Sam.2.29","1Sam.2.30","1Sam.2.31","1Sam.2.32","1Sam.2.33","1Sam.2.34","1Sam.2.35","1Sam.2.36","1Sam.3.11","1Sam.3.13","1Sam.4.17"],"related":[{"id":"eli","type":"cooccur","shared":21,"jaccard":0.42,"why":"21 verses are indexed under bo